the log does not say why. any chance for us to rerun it here? <br><br>On Sat, 2024-07-27 at 10:28 -0700, Ruby Ji wrote:<br>&gt; Dear all,<br>&gt; <br>&gt; I developed a complicated model, that contains multiple SPDE fields and copy<br>&gt; terms:<br>&gt; ...<br>&gt; ## SPDE model ##<br>&gt; spde = inla.spde2.pcmatern(mesh, prior.range = c(diff(range(mesh$loc[, 1])) /<br>&gt; 5, .5), prior.sigma = c(1, 0.5))<br>&gt; <br>&gt; # Observation matrix $A$<br>&gt; table(repl0 &lt;- dat$season - (min(dat$season) - 1))<br>&gt; table(repl1 &lt;- dat$yq - (min(dat$yq) - 1))<br>&gt; A.0 &lt;- inla.spde.make.A(mesh, repl=repl0, loc=as.matrix(dat[,c(&quot;X&quot;,&quot;Y&quot;)]))<br>&gt; A.1 &lt;- inla.spde.make.A(mesh, loc=as.matrix(dat[,c(&quot;X&quot;,&quot;Y&quot;)]), group=dat$yq,<br>&gt; n.group=n.yq)<br>&gt; <br>&gt; # Generating lists of named index vectors for the SPDE models<br>&gt; MIndx0 &lt;- inla.spde.make.index(name=&quot;Mfield0&quot;, n.spde=mesh$n, n.repl=n.season)<br>&gt; MIndx1 &lt;- inla.spde.make.index(name=&quot;Mfield1&quot;, n.spde=mesh$n, n.group=n.yq)<br>&gt; <br>&gt; # Indexes for spatial part<br>&gt; se = sz = sy = MIndx0$Mfield0<br>&gt; sz.1 = sy.1 = MIndx1$Mfield1<br>&gt; <br>&gt; # Indexes for temporal part<br>&gt; re = rz = ry = MIndx0$Mfield0.repl<br>&gt; gz = gy = MIndx1$Mfield1.group<br>&gt; <br>&gt; # Priors for each of the copy parameters are Gaussian with zero mean and<br>&gt; precision 0.001:<br>&gt; hypercopy &lt;- list(theta=list(prior=&quot;normal&quot;, param=c(0, 0.001)))<br>&gt; <br>&gt; # Stack data<br>&gt; stk.e &lt;- inla.stack(tag=&#39;est.e&#39;,<br>&gt;                     data=list(y=cbind(as.vector(e), NA, NA), link=1),<br>&gt;                     A=list(A.0, 1),<br>&gt;                     effects=list(list(se=se, re=re),<br>&gt;                                  list(e.b0=rep(1,length(e)),<br>&gt;                                       season.e=dat$season)))<br>&gt; <br>&gt; stk.z &lt;- inla.stack(tag=&#39;est.z&#39;,<br>&gt;                     data=list(y=cbind(NA, as.vector(z), NA), link=2),<br>&gt;                     A=list(A.1, A.0, 1),<br>&gt;                     effects=list(list(sz.1=sz.1, gz=gz),<br>&gt;                                  list(sz=sz, rz=rz),<br>&gt;                                  list(z.b0=rep(1,length(z)),<br>&gt;                                       yq.z=dat$yq,<br>&gt;                                       season.z=dat$season,<br>&gt;                                       ves.z=dat$ves)))<br>&gt; stk.y &lt;- inla.stack(tag=&#39;est.y&#39;,<br>&gt;                     data=list(y=cbind(NA, NA, as.vector(y)), link=3),<br>&gt;                     A=list(A.1, A.0, 1),<br>&gt;                     effects=list(list(sy.1=sy.1, gy=gy),<br>&gt;                                  list(sy=sy, ry=ry),<br>&gt;                                  list(y.b0=rep(1,length(y)),<br>&gt;                                       yq.y=dat$yq,<br>&gt;                                       season.y=dat$season,<br>&gt;                                       ves.y=dat$ves)))<br>&gt; stk.ezy &lt;- inla.stack(stk.e, stk.z, stk.y)<br>&gt; <br>&gt; <br>&gt; # INLA formula <br>&gt; form &lt;- y ~ 0 + e.b0 + z.b0 + y.b0 + <br>&gt;   f(season.e, model=&#39;iid&#39;, hyper=list(theta=list(param=c(0.1,0.1))),<br>&gt; constr=TRUE) + <br>&gt;   f(se, model=spde, replicate=re) +<br>&gt;   <br>&gt;   f(yq.z, model=&#39;rw1&#39;, hyper = list(theta = list(prior=&quot;pc.prec&quot;,<br>&gt; param=c(0.5,0.01))), scale.model=TRUE, constr=TRUE) + <br>&gt;   f(season.z, copy=&#39;season.e&#39;, fixed = FALSE) + <br>&gt;   f(ves.z, model=&#39;iid&#39;, hyper=list(theta=list(param=c(0.1,0.1))), constr=TRUE)<br>&gt; +<br>&gt;   f(sz.1, model=spde, group=gz, control.group=list(model=&quot;rw1&quot;)) +<br>&gt;   f(sz, copy=&quot;se&quot;, replicate=rz, fixed=FALSE , hyper=hypercopy) +<br>&gt; <br>&gt;   f(yq.y, model=&#39;rw1&#39;, hyper = list(theta = list(prior=&quot;pc.prec&quot;,<br>&gt; param=c(0.5,0.01))), scale.model=TRUE, constr=TRUE) + <br>&gt;   f(season.y, copy=&#39;season.e&#39;, fixed = FALSE) + <br>&gt;   f(ves.y, model=&#39;iid&#39;, hyper=list(theta=list(param=c(0.1,0.1))), constr=TRUE)<br>&gt; +<br>&gt;   f(sy.1, model=spde, group=gy, control.group=list(model=&quot;rw1&quot;)) +<br>&gt;   f(sy, copy=&quot;se&quot;, replicate=ry, fixed=FALSE , hyper=hypercopy)<br>&gt; <br>&gt; <br>&gt; # call INLA <br>&gt; res &lt;- inla(form, family=c(&#39;poisson&#39;, &#39;binomial&#39;, &#39;gamma&#39;),<br>&gt;             data=inla.stack.data(stk.ezy), <br>&gt;             control.compute=list(dic=TRUE, waic=TRUE, cpo=TRUE, config =<br>&gt; TRUE), <br>&gt;             control.inla=list(strategy=&#39;gaussian&#39;, int.strategy=&#39;eb&#39;), <br>&gt;             control.predictor=list(A=inla.stack.A(stk.ezy), compute=TRUE,<br>&gt; link=inla.stack.data(stk.ezy)$link),<br>&gt;             num.threads=5, keep=TRUE, verbose=TRUE, debug=TRUE, safe=FALSE)<br>&gt; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br>&gt; -----------------------------------------------------------<br>&gt; <br>&gt; This model tends to converge on my laptop but crashes on the HPC. I am not<br>&gt; sure if I set something wrong or if it is due to complicated settings.<br>&gt; Followings are some output. Any comments are appreciated.<br>&gt; <br>&gt; Thanks,<br>&gt; Ruby<br>&gt; <br>&gt; This is INLA_24.06.27 built 2024-06-27 02:36:04 UTC.<br>&gt;  - See <a href="http://www.r-inla.org/contact-us" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.r-inla.org/contact-us&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792434991458000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1JbNq4qLTCiVbz12GMA-mJ">www.r-inla.org/contact-us</a> for how to get help.<br>&gt;  - List available models/likelihoods/etc with inla.list.models()<br>&gt;  - Use inla.doc(&lt;NAME&gt;) to 